<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Consciousness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Consciousness"@en .
<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Consciousness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000144> .
<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Consciousness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Consciousness is an inseparable part of all mental processes. It is that part of the mental process that: a) confers a subjective perspective, a phenomenology, an experience of the mental process of which it is a part; and b) intends the object or event that the mental process is about, should such exist; i.e., it confers intentionality on the mental process."@en .
<http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Consciousness> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "http://www.ontologyrepository.com/CommonCoreOntologies/Domain/CognitiveProcessOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
