<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In traditional astronomical usage, civil time is mean solar time as calculated from midnight as the beginning of the Civil Day."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Note that Civil Time Reference System is more accurately represented as a Temporal Reference System that participates in an act of usage that is sanctioned by an appropriate civil authority. As such, it should be represented as a defined class."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Civil Time Reference System"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001328> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Temporal Reference System that is a statutory time scale as designated by civilian authorities to determine local time(s)."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000067> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/InformationEntityOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
