<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000362> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Most rocket engines are also Internal Combustion Engines, however non-combusting forms also exist. For example, an untied balloon full of air that is released and allowed to zoom around the room may be both a Rocket Engine and a Physically Powered Engine."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000362> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Rocket Engine"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000362> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000533> .
