<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000452> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000323> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000452> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An Artifact Function that is realized during events in which an Artifact is used to keep track of and report the current time."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000452> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ArtifactOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000453> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000453> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Controlling air quality typically involves temperature control, oxygen replenishment, and removal of moisture, odor, smoke, heat, dust, airborne bacteria, carbon dioxide, and other undesired gases or particulates."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000453> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Environment Control System"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000453> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000995> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000453> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Material Artifact that is designed to control the temperature, air quality, or other feature of a Site that is relevant to the comfort or operation of entities located within that Site."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000453> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001760> "https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ArtifactOntology"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#anyURI> .
