<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000506> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Role that inheres in an Agent or Group of Agents by virtue of that Agent or Group of Agents entering into a Contract to provide materials or labor to perform a service or complete a task."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000506> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A Contractor Role differs from an Occupation Role in at least two ways. First, the Contract that binds the two parties together is not one of employment. Second, a Contractor Role is occupationally neutral in that an Agent can be contracted to perform any number of Occupational Roles."@en .
