<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000592> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000592> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "'Deviation Measurement Information Content Entity' and 'Veracity Measurement Information Content Entity' are complementary notions. Deviation is a measure of whether reality conforms to an ICE (e.g., a plan or prediction), whereas Veracity is a measure of whether a Descriptive ICE conforms to reality."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000592> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Note, the term 'accuracy' is avoided due to its ambiguity between: correctness-of-performance (see: 'Reliability Measurement Information Content Entity'), correctness-of-information ('Veracity Measurement Information Content Entity'), and adherance-to-expectations (see: 'Deviation Measurement Information Content Entity')."@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000592> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Veracity Measurement Information Content Entity"@en .
<https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00000592> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://www.commoncoreontologies.org/ont00001163> .
